# Barlow-Hall et al. (2023), MNRAS 519, 6055  [arXiv:2201.11139]
# Constraints on the X-ray luminosity function of AGN at z = 5.7-6.4
# with the Extragalactic Serendipitous Swift Survey (ExSeSS).
#
# Redshift bin: 5.7 < z < 6.4, tabulated at the bin centre z = 6.05.
# Band: rest-frame 2-10 keV.  Luminosity bins are 1 dex wide, tabulated
#     at the bin centre.
# Cosmology: flat LCDM, H0 = 70, Om = 0.3, OL = 0.7.
# Phi convention: linear dPhi/dlogLX in Mpc^-3 dex^-1.
#
# Source: their Table 2 (published values, NOT digitised): Phi = 2.98
#     (+6.86, -2.47) x 10^-9. The +/- are the 1-sigma Poisson ERRORS for
#     one detected source (Gehrels 1986: its 1-sigma limits for N = 1 are
#     3.30 and 0.173 times Phi, i.e. +2.30 and -0.83 Phi), so the interval
#     is 0.51e-9 to 9.84e-9; hence Errors = ULDeltas for this dataset.
#
# The authors note these are formally lower limits, since they assume
# no other z > 5.7 sources in ExSeSS.
#
# The 45.8 < logLX < 46.8 bin contains no detections; the
# value below is their 1-sigma UPPER LIMIT on Phi.
#
# logLX  Phi
46.30 2.22e-10
